Groovy Level 4 - OOP (Object-Oriented Programming)

This level is very important because Jenkins Shared Libraries, Spring Boot, and many Java/Groovy projects use OOP concepts.

Topics Covered

✅ Class
 ✅ Object
 ✅ Constructor
 ✅ Methods
 ✅ Inheritance
 ✅ Encapsulation
 ✅ Static Methods

Exercise 1: Create Your First Class

File: student.groovy

Groovy
class Student {
 
String name
 
void display() {
println "Student Name = ${name}"
}
}
 
Student s = new Student()
s.name = "Hyarel"
 
s.display()
Output
Plain Text
Student Name = Hyarel
